15 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Four-panel scientific figure about cacao trait analysis. Panel A summarizes the study design, including repeated-harvest cacao panel, number of accessions, SNPs, harvest periods, and prediction targets. Panel B is a horizontal bar chart showing trait repeatability values for five legacy traits across four harvests, with Flower WBD AUDPC \(log\) having the highest repeatability. Panel C is a line graph showing Branch WBD AUDPC \(log\) trajectories over four harvest periods for four cacao accessions, with each accession represented by a distinct color. Panel D is a heatmap showing Pearson correlation coefficients among five legacy traits, with a color scale from red \(high positive\) to blue \(high negative\), and some \215ns\216 indicating non-significant correlations.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Panel A contains a grouped bar chart comparing blocked cross-validation Pearson r values for different traits in Criollo and Matina, with Criollo generally higher. Panel B shows a scatterplot comparing random versus relatedness-blocked validation Pearson r values for both genotypes, revealing a positive relationship. Panel C presents a grouped bar chart of \205log10 FDR q-values for permutation support after FDR correction, with a dashed significance threshold line and Criollo generally higher. Panel D contains a horizontal bar chart showing gain over the null baseline for traits and genotype combinations, with each bar labeled and the highest gains at the top.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Four-panel scientific figure displaying model comparison metrics for various traits and model specifications. Panel A is a heatmap colored yellow, showing high Spearman correlation coefficients for trajectory concordance across model specifications. Panel B is a heatmap with mostly pink and yellow shades, indicating top-accession overlap \(Jaccard index\) across model specifications. Panel C is a horizontal bar chart labeled \215Trajectory fitting diagnostics\216 displaying warning counts for different trait and model combinations, with Flower WBD Audpc \(Log\) | random intercept slope having the highest count. Panel D is a horizontal bar chart labeled \215Prediction robustness across alternative blocking definitions,\216 showing mean blocked cross-validation Pearson correlation coefficients for various intercept and slope predictions across blocking definitions, with purple, green, and orange bars denoting different traits.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Figure with four panels depicting results from a breeding analysis. Panel A is a bar graph ranking top accessions by selection index with Pareto-optimal bars highlighted. Panel B is a scatterplot showing Pareto-efficient breeding space, highlighting Pareto-optimal accessions. Panel C is a dot plot with error bars illustrating rank stability across weight schemes for selected accessions. Panel D is a heatmap summarizing consensus shortlist stability by various frequency metrics and rank standard deviation, with values color-coded from purple to yellow.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Four-panel data visualization analyzing cross-reference concordance and prediction robustness for Criollo and Matina. Panel A is a scatterplot comparing blocked cross-validation Pearson correlations for disease and yield-related targets between the two marker frameworks. Panel B is a horizontal bar chart showing Criollo-minus-Matina differences in prediction performance, with positive values indicating higher performance under Criollo and negative values indicating higher performance under Matina. Panel C is a scatterplot of observed versus predicted standardized scores for branch WBD intercept, with points colored by reference framework. Panel D is a horizontal bar chart displaying the mean Pearson r across stress tests for the most robust targets, split by reference.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
